bugatti has done the near impossible  with its near sharone this 2.6 million  dollar beast is the successor to the  Veyron and it debuted in Geneva Monday  night this is the 1500 horsepower  w16 supercar that Bugatti says will go  to 60 miles per hour and well under two  and a half seconds  it has 1600 Newton meters of torque with  a two-stage turbo engine and a top speed  of 311 miles per hour or more it's  faster and more powerful than the Veyron  with a totally new stiffer suspension a  new aerodynamic system bigger brakes  bigger wheels and if you can believe it  improved handling and on-road dynamics  but the best part of this new beast is  how bugatti has managed to make it  beautiful - the swooped air vents on the  side the carbon-fiber rear in the square  LED lights on the low front face look  extreme but well finished like an animal  that has learned to combine its sheer  power with the precision of control  you got to make only 500 of them and a  full one-third of those have already  been spoken for  it's rare when the literal best in the  world of luxury design and performance  converge into one object let alone a car  if you see one in the wild count  yourself lucky
 

